I am currently running NetHack 3.1.1 on 
a Sun IPX with SunOS, X11R5 as X server
and olwm as window manager.

My problem is that all of the text on the
map window is displayed only in the foreground 
color.  I have traced the code to the
point where the characters are actually
put to the screen and a printf revealed
that they were indeed supposed to be 
different colors, e.g., 
printing '@' in color 15
printing '%' in color 10

The problem thus appears to be in the initialization of 
the color array?  I do not really understand what
happens when the gc is initialized, so I 
haven't tried to check whether the color
table allocation failed or so on.  What 
seems odd is that I have had no trouble specifying
my own colors for the status areas.

I have checked to make sure that all of the 
appropriate code areas are called (e.g. the
object array initialization, the gc initialization,
the output routines and color macros) and
cannot figure what's going wrong.

Any NetHack hackers out there who can tell me
what's wrong?

